<v Susan Burton>Then there are the collectors, the mint in boxers. By making the dolls collectible, American Girl Place can keep girls buying dolls long past the age they normally would. Their families can be a little spooky. I meet one grandmother who pulls from her handbag photographs of her granddaughter's closet. Yes, photos of a closet, filled with American Girl accessories. The stepgrandmother, who is also in the store, tells me that the girl has everything for Kirsten.
<v Susan Burton>此外还有收藏家，那些玩偶还在包装盒里的收藏家。通过让玩偶具有收藏价值，美国女孩广场可以让女孩在过了正常年龄后继续购买玩偶。她们的家庭可能有点古怪。我见到了一位祖母，她从手提包里拿出她孙女衣橱的照片。是的，衣橱的照片，塞满了美国女孩的配饰。那个同样在店里的继祖母告诉我，那个女孩拥有克里斯汀的一切。

00:12:39.110 --> 00:13:03.990
<v Grandmother>For a while there, she thought that this was too babyish for her, so got out of it. But then I think she has realized that this is something that you collect, and you can just enjoy your whole life, really. I was telling her about Demi Moore, that she has a collection of dolls, and she has a special house for all her dolls. So it's just a nice hobby.
<v Grandmother>有一段时间，她觉得这对她来说太幼稚了，所以不玩了。但我认为她意识到这是一个可以收藏的东西，你可以终身享受它。我告诉她黛米·摩尔的事，说她收藏玩偶，还有一间专门放她所有玩偶的房子。所以这只是一个很好的爱好。

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:16.080
<v Susan Burton>Downstairs on the first floor, Whitney and her mother look at the dioramas. There are glassed-in living rooms filled with period furniture, one for each historic character, and display cases of accessories and clothing.
<v Susan Burton>在楼下的一楼，惠特尼和她的母亲看着立体模型。有带玻璃的客厅，里面摆满了年代家具，每个历史角色一个，还有展示配饰和服装的陈列柜。

