<v Susan Burton>In the musical review-- the theater is just past the dioramas-- the dolls are literally brought to life, channeled through six rosy-cheeked, middle school-age girls who act out stories the audience already knows from the American Girl books.
<v Susan Burton>在音乐剧评论中——剧院就在立体模型旁边——玩偶们被赋予了生命，通过六个红润脸蛋、初中年纪的女孩来演绎，她们表演的都是观众从美国女孩书中早已熟知的故事情节。

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:50.130
<v Susan Burton>After the musical, I have tea with Whitney and her mother. The cafe is elegant, in a cartoonish way. Dark pink carpet, lamps studded with plastic Gerbera daisies, overstuffed striped chairs. There is a harpist playing a Backstreet Boys song. Scones and tea sandwiches are served on tiered platters. Girls sip from iced pink lemonade. They sit up straight. They're giggly and polite.
<v Susan Burton>音乐剧结束后，我和惠特尼还有她妈妈喝了茶。咖啡馆非常优雅，带有一种卡通感。深粉色的地毯，点缀着塑料非洲菊的灯具，填充感十足的条纹椅子。有一个竖琴手在演奏后街男孩的歌曲。司康饼和茶点三明治装在分层盘子里。女孩们抿着冰镇粉红柠檬水。她们坐得很直。她们爱笑而有礼貌。

